{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into perception and motion subsystems to separate uncontrollable sensor events from controllable actions. The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, prioritizing forward motion and random_walk in clear states, and using conservative, one-shot recovery (short turns or rare backward) on obstacles. full_rotate is only enabled after repeated failures. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to clarify uncontrollable vs controllable event handling.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-maximizing actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
